	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "STMicroelectronics ST25R3916-AQET, UFQFPN32, 5.0 x 5.0 x 0.55 mm, 0.50 mm pitch, 32 perimeter lands plus central exposed pad 33. PRIMARY PROVENANCE: ST UFQFPN32 5x5x0.55 RECOMMENDED PCB LAND PATTERN - perimeter land 0.30 wide x 0.75 long, overall recommended-land span 5.30 (so land centres at +/-2.275), central exposed-pad land 3.45 x 3.45 against a 3.50 nominal package EP, package body 5.00 x 5.00. Recommended-land values are used throughout, NOT the raw package terminal dimensions. Applicability: ST designates ST25R3916-AQET as UFQFPN32 5x5x0.55, the same package family. Classification VERIFIED_VENDOR_EXACT_PACKAGE_FAMILY. SECONDARY ONLY: the exact-part LCSC/EasyEDA entry C5267441 gives pitch 0.50, perimeter pads 0.28 x 0.665 and EP 3.50 x 3.50. Its copper does NOT match ST's recommended land and is NOT used - it is an IPC/library alternate. It does corroborate pad count, pitch, body, EP location and numbering/orientation. NOT the AQWT part: AQWT is VFQFPN 5x5x1.0 with wettable flanks and NRND; its geometry is not used here. PASTE: ST does not prescribe an aperture pattern in the package drawing, so the exposed pad carries a conservative 2x2 segmentation of 1.4 x 1.4 apertures on 1.8 mm centres, about 66 percent coverage. That segmentation is ASSEMBLY IMPLEMENTATION, not manufacturer geometry. Thermal vias are deliberately NOT part of this footprint and remain PCB-layout work; ST recommends soldering the exposed pad to PCB ground.")
	(tags "ST ST25R3916 AQET NFC UFQFPN32 QFN32 5x5 0.5mm exposed-pad")
